 "applies_to": "Desert Aire ExpertAire LW wide-temperature-range dehumidifiers (industrial, water treatment, ice rink and grow uses) running program version 2.0.6.",
 "summary": "The ExpertAire LW is a single-compressor dehumidifier for low and wide temperature ranges. Over BACnet the BMS can switch the unit off, command occupancy, write occupied and unoccupied space temperature and RH setpoints, and send its own zone temperature and RH readings. An optional heartbeat (enable, toggle point and delay) supervises the BMS link. Status and alarms are binary values; unit status and zone-sensor source are integer codes.",
 "bacnet_transport": [],
 "firmware": "Program version 2.0.6",
 "default_device_instance": null,
 "access_inferred": false,
 "notes": [
  "BV 8 Active Alarm is inverted: 0 = alarm, 1 = normal.",
  "The list gives many analog values 'in tenths' (two differential pressures in thousandths); check whether your BMS reads 72.5 or 725 and scale if needed.",
  "The source lists instances 1001 and up as type \"INT\" and does not say which BACnet object type that is. They are shown here as AV, but Desert Aire does not confirm that; check the actual object type with a device discovery before mapping.",
  "AV 30/31 show the setpoints actually in use; AV 23-26 are the BMS-written network setpoints.",
  "The source does not say whether the unit uses BACnet IP or BACnet MS/TP."
 ],
